1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,169
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,261 --> 00:00:14,180
<i>So you're the one</i>
<i>tutoring my son for free.</i>

3
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:16,391
<i>You're more beautiful up close.</i>

4
00:00:16,474 --> 00:00:17,642
[Arthur] <i>Did your wife tell you</i>

5
00:00:17,726 --> 00:00:19,310
<i>about what happened yesterday at school?</i>

6
00:00:19,394 --> 00:00:20,645
[Dante] <i>I'll press charges!</i>

7
00:00:20,729 --> 00:00:22,647
[Camia] <i>Please don't stir up trouble.</i>

8
00:00:22,731 --> 00:00:23,982
[Cindy]<i> Slow down, I might slip.</i>

9
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:26,443
-[Raul] <i>Take your shoes off.</i>
-[Cindy] <i>It's slippery.</i>

10
00:00:26,526 --> 00:00:28,236
[tense music playing]

11
00:00:28,319 --> 00:00:30,488
-[Cindy] <i>What is it?</i>
-[gunshot]

12
00:00:30,572 --> 00:00:32,365
-[man 1] <i>The job's done.</i>
-[Emilia] <i>Good job.</i>

13
00:00:32,949 --> 00:00:34,784
<i>Poor Cinderella.</i>

14
00:00:34,868 --> 00:00:36,578
[Julio] <i>It's the talk of the town.</i>

15
00:00:36,661 --> 00:00:40,081
<i>Your devoted husband couldn't</i>
<i>keep his pants on again.</i>

16
00:00:40,165 --> 00:00:41,249
<i>Fix this, Emilia.</i>

17
00:00:41,332 --> 00:00:43,918
<i>Our political enemies</i>
<i>might catch wind of this.</i>

18
00:00:44,002 --> 00:00:46,171
<i>-Yes, Papa.</i>
<i>-That Dante Cruz…</i>

19
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:49,299
<i>He has already aggravated</i>
<i>a friend of mine from Manila.</i>

20
00:00:49,382 --> 00:00:51,426
<i>He's not easy to silence.</i>

21
00:00:51,509 --> 00:00:52,969
[Emilia] <i>I'll take care of him, Papa.</i>

22
00:00:53,052 --> 00:00:55,972
[man] <i>Attorney Cruz, the mayor</i>
<i>is inviting you to her office.</i>

23
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:59,184
<i>-I'm not afraid of you!</i>
<i>-You won't win.</i>

24
00:00:59,267 --> 00:01:00,226
[vehicle crashes]

25
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:03,354
<i>You killed my husband! Get out!</i>

26
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:07,484
[Diego crying]<i> Lily, I'm sorry.</i>
<i>I don't know. I'm sorry, Lily.</i>

27
00:01:07,567 --> 00:01:09,861
[Camia] <i>Who are you?</i>
<i>Don't come any closer.</i>

28
00:01:09,944 --> 00:01:11,529
-[Lily] <i>Mom?</i>
-[Camia] <i>Get out of here.</i>

29
00:01:11,613 --> 00:01:12,822
Hey!

30
00:01:13,615 --> 00:01:15,450
<i>Lily… Run!</i>

31
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:16,659
<i>-No!</i>
-[gunshot]

32
00:01:17,577 --> 00:01:20,663
[sobbing]<i> Help… Help me!</i>

33
00:01:20,747 --> 00:01:26,961
<i>Mom. Mom. Mom. Mom!</i>

34
00:01:28,254 --> 00:01:29,506
<i>Mom!</i>

35
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:37,972
[woman] No, sir. I didn't hear
any gunshot or screaming.

36
00:01:38,056 --> 00:01:39,599
We didn't hear anything.

37
00:01:40,433 --> 00:01:44,854
[police officer] Nothing?
You didn't see anyone come here?

38
00:01:45,522 --> 00:01:46,356
No.

39
00:01:47,148 --> 00:01:48,566
Good morning.

40
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:51,569
I'm Esther from the social
welfare department.

41
00:01:51,653 --> 00:01:54,823
-And he's my colleague.
-Good morning, sir.

42
00:01:54,906 --> 00:01:59,077
We were sent here for a
child named… Lily Cruz.

43
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:03,123
[suspenseful music playing]

44
00:02:07,335 --> 00:02:10,421
-I don't think I can do this.
-This isn't the first time.

45
00:02:10,505 --> 00:02:14,217
You know I don't kill children, right?

46
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:19,472
How about you? Can you kill her?
Let's just set her free!

47
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:22,684
The governor and mayor
will kill us if we let her go.

48
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:24,769
Then think of another way!

49
00:02:26,062 --> 00:02:26,938
[whispers] I can't do this.

50
00:02:27,021 --> 00:02:30,567
[man] Don't tell me
you're feeling guilty now.

51
00:02:30,650 --> 00:02:31,734
[tense music playing]

52
00:02:31,818 --> 00:02:33,903
-Oh, no!
-What?

53
00:02:33,987 --> 00:02:35,780
-[man] Lily!
-Lily!

54
00:02:35,864 --> 00:02:38,032
-Lily! Lily!
-[man] Stop right there!

55
00:02:38,116 --> 00:02:39,742
-Lily! Lily!
-[Esther] Lily!

56
00:02:39,826 --> 00:02:42,787
-[man] Come back!
-Got you!

57
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:44,247
-Please let go!
-Where are you going?

58
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:47,125
Hello, Mayor. Should I dump the body?

59
00:02:52,714 --> 00:02:54,966
-[goon 1] There's a car!
-[goon 2] Relax.

60
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:57,635
-Do you have the child?
-Yes, ma'am.

61
00:02:58,678 --> 00:02:59,762
I want to hear her.

62
00:03:03,349 --> 00:03:07,604
Please don't kill me!
Please have mercy on me.

63
00:03:08,479 --> 00:03:09,355
-[Lily] I'm begging you.
-Hello?

64
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:12,942
You know what to do. Finish her off.

65
00:03:15,486 --> 00:03:18,197
[sobbing] Please let me go!

66
00:03:18,281 --> 00:03:20,742
Mister, don't kill me.

67
00:03:22,035 --> 00:03:23,036
[gunshot]

68
00:03:30,835 --> 00:03:33,838
-[slow instrumental music playing]
-[rain pouring]

69
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:38,343
[sobbing]

70
00:03:40,637 --> 00:03:42,388
Get up. Listen.

71
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:47,352
You have to get away from here. Go.

72
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:51,272
[man] Just don't tell the police.

73
00:03:51,356 --> 00:03:55,318
Don't tell anyone. No matter what happens…

74
00:03:56,194 --> 00:03:58,988
don't ever come back
to Poblacion Ardiente.

75
00:03:59,072 --> 00:04:00,323
Understood?

76
00:04:01,032 --> 00:04:04,202
-Hurry! Run!
-[Esther] Go now!

77
00:04:08,289 --> 00:04:09,874
-[man] Alma…
-[Alma] Yes?

78
00:04:09,958 --> 00:04:13,628
[man] I need another basket
for my next trip here.

79
00:04:14,337 --> 00:04:15,421
[Alma] Okay.

80
00:04:18,967 --> 00:04:20,969
[man] Is that everything, Philip?

81
00:04:21,052 --> 00:04:24,430
Let's get the rest so we can leave soon.

82
00:04:24,514 --> 00:04:27,642
[ambulance siren wailing]

83
00:04:28,351 --> 00:04:30,019
[tense music playing]

84
00:04:37,568 --> 00:04:39,279
[man] I like that tree's fruits.

85
00:04:39,362 --> 00:04:43,032
-[Alma] Okay. Take care.
-[man] See you.

86
00:04:58,881 --> 00:05:01,050
[engine roaring]

87
00:05:07,724 --> 00:05:11,102
[Loring] It's deserted. What happened?

88
00:05:11,185 --> 00:05:13,896
Diego, don't go in there! Just stay here.

89
00:05:14,731 --> 00:05:16,524
Why is it closed off?

90
00:05:17,775 --> 00:05:20,153
Oh, hey! Excuse me, miss!

91
00:05:21,738 --> 00:05:26,075
-Do you know what happened here?
-We aren't sure, either.

92
00:05:26,159 --> 00:05:29,746
They didn't see a body
or anything. Nothing at all.

93
00:05:29,829 --> 00:05:32,457
Where's Mrs. Camia?

94
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:33,958
It's been two days,

95
00:05:34,042 --> 00:05:37,128
but we haven't even caught
a glimpse of her.

96
00:05:37,211 --> 00:05:42,550
-I think she's dead.
-No. No. Don't say that!

97
00:05:42,633 --> 00:05:45,386
-What about Lily?
-[woman] Oh, Lily.

98
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:48,473
The social workers
took her away yesterday.

99
00:05:48,556 --> 00:05:50,099
Back to Manila.

100
00:05:51,893 --> 00:05:54,395
[Raul's phone ringing]

101
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:59,484
-Hey, Diego.
-[Diego crying] <i>Daddy?</i>

102
00:05:59,567 --> 00:06:02,361
-We're at Lily's.
-[Raul] <i>Didn't I tell you</i>

103
00:06:02,445 --> 00:06:04,030
not to go to that place anymore?

104
00:06:04,113 --> 00:06:07,867
There's tape that says
"Police Line Do Not Cross" here.

105
00:06:07,950 --> 00:06:10,661
I'm worried that Mrs. Camia may be dead.

106
00:06:11,579 --> 00:06:13,623
<i>Lily's gone too.</i>

107
00:06:13,706 --> 00:06:16,959
The social workers took her to Manila.

108
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:21,130
-They took her to Manila right away?
-[Diego] <i>Yes.</i>

109
00:06:21,214 --> 00:06:24,008
Daddy, you know a lot of cops, right?

110
00:06:24,092 --> 00:06:25,927
<i>Let's find Lily.</i>

111
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:29,514
I'm sure she needs our help right now.

112
00:06:30,139 --> 00:06:31,099
You know, Diego…

113
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:35,394
It's better if…
you don't expect to see Lily again.

114
00:06:35,478 --> 00:06:36,854
What?

115
00:06:38,481 --> 00:06:41,484
[melancholic music playing]

116
00:06:45,321 --> 00:06:48,282
He said I won't see Lily again.

117
00:06:48,991 --> 00:06:50,993
[slow upbeat music playing]

118
00:06:52,578 --> 00:06:55,581
[street noise]

119
00:07:02,171 --> 00:07:04,465
[indistinct chatter]

120
00:07:08,344 --> 00:07:11,097
We need to hurry up, okay?

121
00:07:14,725 --> 00:07:17,353
What the heck is this?! Who are you?!

122
00:07:18,646 --> 00:07:22,066
For Pete's sake! That's been weighed!

123
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:25,111
-[Lily] I'm sorry, sir.
-Explain this to my boss!

124
00:07:25,194 --> 00:07:28,114
I'm really sorry! I didn't mean to!

125
00:07:28,197 --> 00:07:30,867
-Hey, come back here! Hey, kid!
-I'm really sorry, sir!

126
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:32,952
[Lily panting]

127
00:07:40,084 --> 00:07:41,085
Kid.

128
00:07:41,919 --> 00:07:42,962
Need a ride? Where to?

129
00:07:44,922 --> 00:07:45,923
I don't.

130
00:07:47,091 --> 00:07:50,470
Sir… Can I ask you something?

131
00:07:50,553 --> 00:07:53,347
Do you know the way to San Marcelino?

132
00:07:53,431 --> 00:07:55,057
-How do I get there?
-Of course, I do!

133
00:07:56,434 --> 00:07:59,645
Can you please tell me how to get there?

134
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:01,230
I'll walk to it.

135
00:08:01,314 --> 00:08:04,609
-It's too far! You'll get lost.
-I don't have money.

136
00:08:04,692 --> 00:08:06,736
Just tell me how to get there.

137
00:08:06,819 --> 00:08:08,112
[tricycle driver] It's all right.

138
00:08:08,196 --> 00:08:09,697
I can walk.

139
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:13,034
You'll get lost!
It's all right! Hop in, come on.

140
00:08:24,003 --> 00:08:27,298
-Mister, what is this place?
-Wait here.

141
00:08:27,381 --> 00:08:29,800
-Why, what's happening?
-I need to get something.

142
00:08:29,884 --> 00:08:32,845
Are we there yet? Get what?

143
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:35,890
I'll just get something. Move a little.

144
00:08:35,973 --> 00:08:38,809
-Sir, I have to go.
-Stay. It won't take long.

145
00:08:38,893 --> 00:08:41,521
-I don't?
-Stay. Let's talk a bit.

146
00:08:41,604 --> 00:08:43,356
I thought you were getting something.

147
00:08:43,439 --> 00:08:44,482
I'm tired. Let's rest here.

148
00:08:44,565 --> 00:08:47,193
I'll get off here. I'll just walk.

149
00:08:47,276 --> 00:08:49,946
-You smell like mangoes.
-[Lily] What? Are you okay?

150
00:08:50,029 --> 00:08:51,155
[tricycle driver] This won't take long.
Hey!

151
00:08:51,239 --> 00:08:53,574
Hey! Get away from me, please. Hey!

152
00:08:54,492 --> 00:08:56,494
-[Lily] <i>Mom, what happened to you?</i>
-[Camia shushes]

153
00:08:56,577 --> 00:08:57,954
-<i>Hey!</i>
-[Camia] <i>Hurry!</i>

154
00:08:58,037 --> 00:08:59,956
-Mister, let go of me!
-Come on, kid.

155
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:01,999
Let go of me.
Mister, I'm going to go down!

156
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:03,793
[tricycle driver] Come on.

157
00:09:03,876 --> 00:09:06,003
[screams] Mom!

158
00:09:06,087 --> 00:09:08,214
-Stay here!
-No! Please!

159
00:09:08,297 --> 00:09:09,590
-Get in.
-Let me go!

160
00:09:09,674 --> 00:09:11,676
[tricycle driver] You're a fighter, huh?

161
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:16,013
[Jepoy blows whistle loudly]

162
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:19,850
[dramatic music playing]

163
00:09:30,111 --> 00:09:32,488
[Jepoy blows whistle]

164
00:09:34,615 --> 00:09:35,992
Are you okay?

165
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:39,870
Obviously, you're not.

166
00:09:39,954 --> 00:09:41,080
[quiet music playing]

167
00:09:41,831 --> 00:09:43,249
-Come here.
-Don't touch me!

168
00:09:43,332 --> 00:09:46,210
Suit yourself, you snob!

169
00:09:51,674 --> 00:09:53,009
[Jepoy blows whistle]

170
00:09:55,136 --> 00:09:57,096
Here. Put that on.

171
00:10:03,227 --> 00:10:06,230
I'll help you out. You really are a snob.

172
00:10:07,815 --> 00:10:10,401
There are lots of thugs around here.

173
00:10:12,486 --> 00:10:13,362
Here.

174
00:10:13,446 --> 00:10:16,782
If you're in trouble, blow this.

175
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:24,290
Anyway, I gotta go. I'm the parking boy!

176
00:10:24,373 --> 00:10:28,461
Jepoy. Just ask around, they know me!

177
00:10:35,551 --> 00:10:38,012
[sullen music playing]

178
00:10:38,095 --> 00:10:39,930
[sobbing]

179
00:10:46,354 --> 00:10:49,190
[car horn honking]

180
00:10:51,901 --> 00:10:54,487
-[sobbing]
-[car horns honking]

181
00:11:03,704 --> 00:11:06,040
-[car horn honking]
-[tires squealing]

182
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:15,299
[Emilia] Leave the bags there.

183
00:11:24,266 --> 00:11:25,518
Shopping spree?

184
00:11:26,227 --> 00:11:27,269
I was stressed.

185
00:11:27,353 --> 00:11:29,688
Why? Is your conscience getting to you?

186
00:11:30,731 --> 00:11:32,358
You're sick.

187
00:11:32,441 --> 00:11:35,319
You killed them all off? A whole family?

188
00:11:36,195 --> 00:11:40,241
Isn't that what you wanted?
I'm just being a good wife.

189
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:46,747
Diego said social workers
picked up the kid, Lily.

190
00:11:46,831 --> 00:11:50,584
Were they really? Or was that another job?

191
00:11:51,919 --> 00:11:52,962
[exhales]

192
00:11:54,296 --> 00:11:57,633
Can you please stop acting
like you have a conscience?

193
00:11:57,716 --> 00:11:58,926
Because it doesn't suit you!

194
00:11:59,009 --> 00:12:00,094
Are you still human?

195
00:12:01,429 --> 00:12:03,597
You didn't even spare the kid.

196
00:12:03,681 --> 00:12:06,976
You don't have the right
to lecture me about a conscience!

197
00:12:07,059 --> 00:12:09,395
Don't be a hypocrite
because you're just as guilty!

198
00:12:09,478 --> 00:12:11,647
And besides, you should be happy

199
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:14,150
because that family's all together now.

200
00:12:26,912 --> 00:12:29,457
[slow instrumental playing]

201
00:12:33,043 --> 00:12:35,129
[car horn honking]

202
00:12:46,432 --> 00:12:48,350
[panting]

203
00:12:50,686 --> 00:12:51,937
[chuckles]

204
00:12:52,021 --> 00:12:54,398
Thank goodness you're awake.

205
00:12:54,482 --> 00:12:59,403
Uh… I'm Carlotta, by the way.

206
00:13:00,154 --> 00:13:05,201
Ms. Prianka said you weren't hurt,
you just fainted.

207
00:13:06,911 --> 00:13:11,790
Okay, I'll let you eat first.
I'll check back on you later.

208
00:13:15,377 --> 00:13:18,130
[suspenseful music playing]

209
00:13:41,195 --> 00:13:42,446
How are you feeling?

210
00:13:43,906 --> 00:13:45,074
[sighs]

211
00:13:46,242 --> 00:13:49,703
I'm asking you how you're feeling.

212
00:13:52,289 --> 00:13:53,374
Oh, well.

213
00:13:53,457 --> 00:13:57,753
I won't waste my time on someone

214
00:13:57,836 --> 00:14:00,965
who doesn't want to talk.

215
00:14:06,762 --> 00:14:09,974
-[stutters] I have to go.
-Go ahead.

216
00:14:10,057 --> 00:14:12,518
The doors are wide open.

217
00:14:14,019 --> 00:14:16,438
You didn't run me over?

218
00:14:16,981 --> 00:14:18,607
No.

219
00:14:18,691 --> 00:14:20,317
You passed out right on time.

220
00:14:20,401 --> 00:14:22,278
Probably because of hunger,

221
00:14:22,361 --> 00:14:23,487
or because of--

222
00:14:26,407 --> 00:14:27,658
You smell awful.

223
00:14:27,741 --> 00:14:29,743
When was the last time you took a bath?

224
00:14:29,827 --> 00:14:31,579
-[comical music playing]
-[Prianka exhales]

225
00:14:31,662 --> 00:14:34,498
Excuse me, I need air.

226
00:14:40,504 --> 00:14:42,506
[slow instrumental playing]

227
00:14:45,175 --> 00:14:50,097
Sweetie, ma'am asked you to take a shower
and brush your teeth.

228
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:52,766
I'll get you a change of clothes.

229
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:55,060
[water dripping]

230
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:04,445
[dramatic music playing]

231
00:15:06,238 --> 00:15:09,325
[Camia] <i>We'll go away.</i>
<i>That's what we should do.</i>

232
00:15:10,326 --> 00:15:13,329
-[Camia] <i>Lily… Run!</i>
-[Lily crying] <i>Mom.</i>

233
00:15:15,289 --> 00:15:18,500
[Lily] <i>Get off me! Help! Help!</i>

234
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:22,129
Mom…

235
00:15:22,212 --> 00:15:25,049
Little girl? I'm coming in.

236
00:15:26,550 --> 00:15:28,218
Are you crying?

237
00:15:29,345 --> 00:15:31,764
What happened to you? Hold on.

238
00:15:31,847 --> 00:15:34,141
-Don't touch me!
-Wait, it's okay! It's okay.

239
00:15:34,224 --> 00:15:37,227
Get away! Please let me go!

240
00:15:37,311 --> 00:15:40,314
-What's happening here?
-Let me go…

241
00:15:40,397 --> 00:15:41,732
[whimpering]

242
00:15:42,358 --> 00:15:48,614
-[Carlotta] Hush now.
-[hallucinating] Mom. Dad.

243
00:15:48,697 --> 00:15:50,240
Mom.

244
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:53,160
[Carlotta humming]

245
00:15:53,243 --> 00:15:54,870
[Carlotta shushes]

246
00:15:57,706 --> 00:15:58,791
I'll take care of her, Carlotta.

247
00:15:58,874 --> 00:16:01,752
-Ma'am?
-I can look after a kid, Carlotta.

248
00:16:09,969 --> 00:16:11,261
Mom.

249
00:16:15,432 --> 00:16:19,353
Ardiente. Ardiente.

250
00:16:20,479 --> 00:16:21,897
Ardiente.

251
00:16:22,648 --> 00:16:24,149
Mayor.

252
00:16:25,234 --> 00:16:29,154
Governor Ardiente.

253
00:16:32,908 --> 00:16:37,788
-[Prianka] It's okay.
-Ardiente. The Ardientes…

254
00:16:38,706 --> 00:16:41,959
[dramatic music playing]

255
00:17:00,144 --> 00:17:02,396
[slow instrumental music playing]

256
00:17:08,652 --> 00:17:10,404
[water dripping]

257
00:17:18,328 --> 00:17:19,371
Mom?

258
00:17:23,083 --> 00:17:24,084
I'm not your mother.

259
00:17:25,919 --> 00:17:27,921
Thank you for taking care of me.

260
00:17:28,839 --> 00:17:30,799
-You're really kind.
-[scoffs]

261
00:17:32,217 --> 00:17:33,594
I'm not kind.

262
00:17:33,677 --> 00:17:35,471
I just don't want anyone
dying on my watch.

263
00:17:36,930 --> 00:17:38,348
[Carlotta clears throat]

264
00:17:40,559 --> 00:17:43,729
-You're in charge of her.
-Yes, ma'am.

265
00:17:44,688 --> 00:17:46,023
Are you feeling better?

266
00:17:46,815 --> 00:17:47,983
Hmm?

267
00:17:49,068 --> 00:17:50,277
Come here.

268
00:17:51,361 --> 00:17:54,114
Let's lift your head a little. That's it.

269
00:17:57,159 --> 00:17:58,494
Just a sip, sweetie.

270
00:18:02,831 --> 00:18:07,669
[Loring] Finish your food
before they arrive. You know how it is.

271
00:18:08,670 --> 00:18:10,422
Thanks, Nanny.

272
00:18:11,256 --> 00:18:14,009
Whenever I think about Lily…

273
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:17,262
I just get hungrier.

274
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:23,727
Why don't the social workers
in Manila know where Lily is?

275
00:18:23,811 --> 00:18:26,063
I don't know, either.

276
00:18:26,146 --> 00:18:31,360
Now finish your food.
We'll call them again later.

277
00:18:31,443 --> 00:18:32,444
[cheerful music playing]

278
00:18:36,615 --> 00:18:37,950
-Nanny!
-[Loring] Yes?

279
00:18:38,033 --> 00:18:42,412
I know how to find Lily!
Come with me, quick!

280
00:18:42,496 --> 00:18:43,372
Okay.

281
00:18:43,455 --> 00:18:44,414
[Diego on television] <i>My name is…</i>

282
00:18:44,498 --> 00:18:46,667
<i>Diego Ardiente-Torillo.</i>

283
00:18:47,626 --> 00:18:53,006
<i>I'm the son of Mayor Emilia,</i>
<i>and the grandson of Governor Julio.</i>

284
00:18:53,757 --> 00:18:58,011
<i>I called social services in Manila.</i>

285
00:18:58,095 --> 00:19:01,557
<i>My best friend Lily Cruz</i>
<i>isn't there either.</i>

286
00:19:02,724 --> 00:19:08,480
<i>To the people who know where Lily is,</i>

287
00:19:08,564 --> 00:19:10,691
<i>please call me</i>

288
00:19:10,774 --> 00:19:15,821
<i>or my nanny at 627-3256.</i>

289
00:19:15,904 --> 00:19:19,658
<i>Lily, I'm really worried.</i>

290
00:19:20,450 --> 00:19:22,578
<i>Come back to Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

291
00:19:25,664 --> 00:19:27,749
[Prianka] Murderous social workers?

292
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:31,253
[Lily crying] Yes, I heard them talk.

293
00:19:31,336 --> 00:19:35,382
It was Mayor Emilia who wanted me killed.

294
00:19:35,465 --> 00:19:41,013
I think they let me escape
because they felt sorry for me.

295
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:46,768
I came to Manila to find my uncle.

296
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:49,938
[stutters] But…

297
00:19:51,481 --> 00:19:53,483
But the tricycle driver…

298
00:19:54,401 --> 00:19:58,113
-[sobbing] The driver…
-[shushes]

299
00:20:00,824 --> 00:20:02,618
[Carlotta] Just stay here, dear.

300
00:20:02,701 --> 00:20:04,870
It's too dangerous for you to go back.

301
00:20:05,871 --> 00:20:07,956
You're safe here, okay?

302
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:10,834
[Emilia] <i>Don't worry.</i>

303
00:20:10,918 --> 00:20:15,672
I assure you I spoke
to that child Lily Cruz myself.

304
00:20:16,298 --> 00:20:18,425
Yes. Thank you. Goodbye.

305
00:20:20,761 --> 00:20:22,638
That was the head
of social services in Manila.

306
00:20:22,721 --> 00:20:24,848
They're trying to trace
where Lily Cruz is,

307
00:20:24,932 --> 00:20:26,183
because of what your son did!

308
00:20:26,266 --> 00:20:29,186
Now we're involved in a scandal.

309
00:20:29,895 --> 00:20:31,939
That issue should've died already!

310
00:20:32,022 --> 00:20:34,066
Good afternoon, Grandpa.

311
00:20:35,359 --> 00:20:37,069
-You idiot!
-What did I do, Grandpa?

312
00:20:37,694 --> 00:20:40,280
You caused a huge scandal!

313
00:20:40,364 --> 00:20:42,824
Because of you,
people are talking about a child

314
00:20:42,908 --> 00:20:46,662
who's gone missing
from Poblacion Ardiente!

315
00:20:47,663 --> 00:20:49,831
-And you.
-[Diego crying]

316
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:54,878
I'm talking to you! Stand up.

317
00:20:56,880 --> 00:21:00,384
Aren't you using your brain?!

318
00:21:00,467 --> 00:21:02,803
Didn't you realize
you could get us all in trouble

319
00:21:02,886 --> 00:21:05,222
by going to the TV station?

320
00:21:05,305 --> 00:21:06,306
-But sir--
-Huh?

321
00:21:07,057 --> 00:21:08,850
[Loring whimpering]

322
00:21:09,518 --> 00:21:11,728
Why are your eyes closed? Open your eyes.

323
00:21:11,812 --> 00:21:14,648
Open them! Open them!

324
00:21:16,108 --> 00:21:18,819
-So you can see where this comes from!
-[Diego] Grandpa!

325
00:21:18,902 --> 00:21:21,530
[Julio] All you two ever bring is trouble!

326
00:21:21,613 --> 00:21:23,490
-[Loring squealing]
-[Diego] Stop it, Grandpa!

327
00:21:23,573 --> 00:21:24,491
Huh?

328
00:21:24,574 --> 00:21:27,286
-You two belong together!
-Grandpa.

329
00:21:27,369 --> 00:21:30,038
-[Loring squealing]
-[Diego wailing]

330
00:21:30,122 --> 00:21:32,165
Papa, that's enough! Your heart!

331
00:21:32,249 --> 00:21:36,795
You looked pathetic asking
for help on national television!

332
00:21:36,878 --> 00:21:37,796
I'm sorry, Grandpa.

333
00:21:37,879 --> 00:21:39,881
Diego! You don't get it, do you?

334
00:21:39,965 --> 00:21:42,426
You always bring disgrace to this family!

335
00:21:42,509 --> 00:21:44,928
Why did you even mention
you were an Ardiente?!

336
00:21:45,012 --> 00:21:48,473
Because that's my last name.

337
00:21:48,557 --> 00:21:52,394
Because of what you did,
we are involved in a crime.

338
00:21:53,186 --> 00:21:57,274
I really don't understand
how you can be an Ardiente.

339
00:21:58,483 --> 00:22:01,611
You're the only disgrace to this family.

340
00:22:03,822 --> 00:22:06,366
[Diego wailing]

341
00:22:11,496 --> 00:22:14,541
That's enough. Come here. Stand up.

342
00:22:15,250 --> 00:22:16,626
[Diego sobbing]

343
00:22:18,587 --> 00:22:19,588
Don't cry.

344
00:22:21,840 --> 00:22:23,759
Take care of him.

345
00:22:25,802 --> 00:22:27,012
Go.

346
00:22:27,804 --> 00:22:30,849
[sullen music playing]

347
00:22:33,268 --> 00:22:34,102
[Diego coughing]

348
00:22:35,562 --> 00:22:38,356
Seriously? Are you crying again?

349
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:41,401
It's true! You don't act like an Ardiente.

350
00:22:41,485 --> 00:22:44,780
There's no weak Ardiente.

351
00:22:45,489 --> 00:22:49,326
I was born an Ardiente. I am an Ardiente.

352
00:22:50,786 --> 00:22:53,663
And I'm going to prove it.

353
00:22:53,747 --> 00:22:54,831
[Arnaldo] Sure!

354
00:22:54,915 --> 00:22:56,958
After you stop being fat.

355
00:23:03,757 --> 00:23:05,509
[Julio] <i>I really don't understand</i>

356
00:23:05,592 --> 00:23:07,260
<i>how you can be an Ardiente.</i>

357
00:23:07,344 --> 00:23:10,472
<i>You're the only disgrace to this family.</i>

358
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:14,351
[Arnaldo] <i>There is no weak Ardiente.</i>

359
00:23:16,645 --> 00:23:21,733
[Diego] <i>I'm an Ardiente,</i>
<i>and I'm going to prove it.</i>

360
00:23:25,821 --> 00:23:29,574
Thank you for everything.
But I need to go.

361
00:23:29,658 --> 00:23:30,784
Then what?

362
00:23:31,743 --> 00:23:33,745
You'll go back to Poblacion Ardiente?

363
00:23:34,913 --> 00:23:38,166
I need to know what happened to my mother.

364
00:23:39,626 --> 00:23:41,128
Don't you know what happened to your mom?

365
00:23:42,462 --> 00:23:43,797
She's dead.

366
00:23:44,506 --> 00:23:48,093
She was killed by the same
people that wanted you dead.

367
00:23:48,677 --> 00:23:50,137
[crying] That's not true!

368
00:23:51,179 --> 00:23:54,683
She's still alive! I can feel it!

369
00:23:54,766 --> 00:23:58,353
When I go back,
I'll know what happened to her.

370
00:23:58,436 --> 00:24:00,438
-When I go back--
-When you go back,

371
00:24:00,522 --> 00:24:02,566
you'll be murdered.

372
00:24:06,319 --> 00:24:09,739
You'll suffer the same fate
as your mother.

373
00:24:10,365 --> 00:24:14,035
Maybe worse than your mother.

374
00:24:15,787 --> 00:24:18,623
So stop it, Lily. Your mom is dead.

375
00:24:18,707 --> 00:24:20,167
That's not true!

376
00:24:20,250 --> 00:24:21,835
You don't know what you're saying!

377
00:24:21,918 --> 00:24:24,713
You don't know anything! That's not true!

378
00:24:25,297 --> 00:24:26,756
You don't know anything!

379
00:24:30,260 --> 00:24:32,012
[Lily sobbing]

380
00:24:33,013 --> 00:24:33,889
Come with me.

381
00:24:33,972 --> 00:24:35,891
[Carlotta] Ms. Prianka.

382
00:24:35,974 --> 00:24:37,642
-Come!
-[Lily] Please let me go.

383
00:24:38,602 --> 00:24:42,355
[Carlotta] Ms. Prianka.
Have mercy on her. Ms. Prianka.

384
00:24:44,024 --> 00:24:48,820
Look! That's the grave of my daughter!

385
00:24:50,113 --> 00:24:52,365
Yes, that's my child!

386
00:24:53,325 --> 00:24:57,787
She died because I wanted justice

387
00:24:57,871 --> 00:25:00,332
for the assassination of my husband.

388
00:25:01,458 --> 00:25:04,669
I went to war unprepared.

389
00:25:06,004 --> 00:25:10,800
And until now, I cannot forgive myself

390
00:25:13,094 --> 00:25:16,223
for the death of my daughter.

391
00:25:16,306 --> 00:25:17,641
[sobbing]

392
00:25:21,728 --> 00:25:27,025
So don't you dare tell me
I don't know anything.

393
00:25:27,108 --> 00:25:30,362
This is what I know.

394
00:25:32,197 --> 00:25:37,244
You can't go back to Ardiente
while you're still weak.

395
00:25:37,327 --> 00:25:41,539
You need to be ready
and strong when you face them.

396
00:25:43,541 --> 00:25:45,710
Your mom and dad are both dead, Lily.

397
00:25:47,420 --> 00:25:48,421
[whimpers]

398
00:25:49,089 --> 00:25:52,425
Whether you like it or not,
you have to accept that.

399
00:25:52,509 --> 00:25:54,010
Now, I ask you.

400
00:25:55,220 --> 00:25:56,471
What do you want?

401
00:25:57,847 --> 00:26:00,267
Do you want to follow them to the grave?

402
00:26:00,350 --> 00:26:03,353
[pensive music playing]

403
00:26:03,436 --> 00:26:06,523
So, what do you want, Lily? Is that it?

404
00:26:10,277 --> 00:26:13,947
I want to make them pay
for what they did to us.

405
00:26:16,241 --> 00:26:17,575
I can't hear you.

406
00:26:18,702 --> 00:26:22,163
I want to make the Ardientes
pay for what they did to us.

407
00:26:23,373 --> 00:26:25,166
I still can't hear you.

408
00:26:26,042 --> 00:26:29,087
I want justice for my mom and dad!

409
00:26:29,170 --> 00:26:30,088
Again?

410
00:26:31,172 --> 00:26:34,968
I want justice for my parents!

411
00:26:37,095 --> 00:26:37,929
Good.

412
00:26:40,223 --> 00:26:41,641
Then we have a deal.

413
00:26:41,725 --> 00:26:44,185
[dramatic music playing]

414
00:26:55,322 --> 00:26:57,115
[instrumental theme music playing]

415
00:27:22,432 --> 00:27:24,059
[Lily] <i>The Count of Monte Cristo.</i>

416
00:27:24,809 --> 00:27:27,645
<i>It's my favorite book.</i>

417
00:27:27,729 --> 00:27:31,691
[instrumental theme music playing]

418
00:27:33,193 --> 00:27:37,822
-[Lily] 365 Days?
-For a year filled with love.

419
00:27:38,948 --> 00:27:43,495
[instrumental theme music playing]

420
00:27:47,916 --> 00:27:48,917
Mom…

421
00:27:50,752 --> 00:27:52,003
Dad…

422
00:27:52,670 --> 00:27:57,759
[instrumental theme music playing]

423
00:28:18,279 --> 00:28:20,949
That's it. Cry it all out.

424
00:28:23,243 --> 00:28:25,245
Bury your memories of them.

425
00:28:27,205 --> 00:28:30,041
If you want my help,

426
00:28:30,667 --> 00:28:33,545
you will do what I say.

427
00:28:33,628 --> 00:28:35,630
[exhales] I will.

428
00:28:37,674 --> 00:28:39,759
Put all of them in the box.

429
00:28:42,345 --> 00:28:43,680
[sobbing]

430
00:28:44,472 --> 00:28:45,557
Now!

431
00:28:47,767 --> 00:28:49,561
[sobs]

432
00:28:54,441 --> 00:28:58,111
[dramatic music playing]

433
00:29:12,959 --> 00:29:14,127
[Prianka] Bury it.

434
00:29:14,627 --> 00:29:15,587
Now!

435
00:29:28,099 --> 00:29:30,935
Wipe your tears. Stop crying!

436
00:29:55,168 --> 00:29:56,461
[Lily] What is this?

437
00:29:57,295 --> 00:29:59,839
Open and read it.

438
00:30:01,424 --> 00:30:03,468
I'm keeping my end of the bargain.

439
00:30:04,302 --> 00:30:09,849
I've legally adopted you.
You'll be called… Ivy Aguas.

440
00:30:09,933 --> 00:30:10,809
[quiet music playing]

441
00:30:10,892 --> 00:30:14,479
From now on, that is your birthday.

442
00:30:14,562 --> 00:30:18,107
The day you arrived in my house.

443
00:30:20,985 --> 00:30:23,112
-Uh…
-A simple thank you will do.

444
00:30:23,822 --> 00:30:25,824
[stutters] Thank you.

445
00:30:27,826 --> 00:30:30,370
[instrumental theme music playing]

446
00:30:31,996 --> 00:30:33,832
[Carlotta chuckles]

447
00:30:39,921 --> 00:30:41,256
[Prianka] Make sure to do me proud.

448
00:30:41,339 --> 00:30:44,634
Don't let me down
because you carry my name.

449
00:30:49,180 --> 00:30:51,474
Something grew.

450
00:30:53,893 --> 00:30:54,894
Yes.

451
00:30:55,895 --> 00:30:58,648
A lone blossom.

452
00:30:58,731 --> 00:31:00,316
A wildflower.

453
00:31:03,027 --> 00:31:04,654
[Ivy] What's it called?

454
00:31:05,613 --> 00:31:06,990
I don't know.

455
00:31:10,660 --> 00:31:13,079
But that's not important.

456
00:31:20,086 --> 00:31:23,423
What's important
is it can thrive anywhere.

457
00:31:24,632 --> 00:31:29,929
It can survive
in the midst of any weather…

458
00:31:31,973 --> 00:31:34,684
with no one taking care of it.

459
00:31:35,685 --> 00:31:39,188
It doesn't let the world bring it down.

460
00:31:41,649 --> 00:31:45,236
[instrumental theme music playing]

461
00:31:47,947 --> 00:31:51,200
And I hope you grow up to be like one.

462
00:31:56,039 --> 00:31:57,999
First, a napkin.

463
00:31:59,042 --> 00:32:02,253
It's very important to keep
your posture straight at all times.

464
00:32:02,337 --> 00:32:05,173
These are for water,
red wine, and white wine.

465
00:32:05,256 --> 00:32:08,051
For the appetizer… For the soup.

466
00:32:09,719 --> 00:32:12,931
No, Ivy. This way.

467
00:32:18,102 --> 00:32:19,103
Good, right?

468
00:32:20,480 --> 00:32:22,357
Go! Go, Ivy!

469
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:27,612
[Ivy] <i>This was the only way</i>
<i>for me to be reborn.</i>

470
00:32:28,196 --> 00:32:30,907
<i>To fulfill my new dreams.</i>

471
00:32:30,990 --> 00:32:33,409
<i>Become a new me.</i>

472
00:32:33,493 --> 00:32:34,410
[Prianka] There.

473
00:32:34,494 --> 00:32:37,163
Change! Protect yourself.

474
00:32:37,246 --> 00:32:40,583
[Ivy] <i>There are times</i>
<i>I still think about them…</i>

475
00:32:40,667 --> 00:32:45,046
<i>or dream of seeing them,</i>
<i>even in a picture.</i>

476
00:32:45,129 --> 00:32:49,634
<i>I'm scared that I might forget</i>
<i>their faces,</i>

477
00:32:49,717 --> 00:32:51,844
<i>the memories of my family.</i>

478
00:32:52,679 --> 00:32:56,808
<i>But Ms. Prianka did say that,</i>
<i>if I want justice…</i>

479
00:32:57,517 --> 00:33:00,061
<i>I need to be patient.</i>

480
00:33:00,144 --> 00:33:04,023
[tense music playing]

481
00:33:18,246 --> 00:33:19,163
[boy grunts]

482
00:33:23,876 --> 00:33:26,838
[dramatic music playing]

483
00:33:36,889 --> 00:33:38,808
[both grunt]

484
00:33:47,567 --> 00:33:49,110
[guy groans]

485
00:33:52,989 --> 00:33:55,033
Proud of yourself, are you?

486
00:33:55,116 --> 00:33:57,493
Were you expecting me to applaud you?

487
00:33:58,870 --> 00:34:03,458
You should know better, Ivy.
Get dressed. We're leaving.

488
00:34:03,541 --> 00:34:05,960
There are a lot of things
you still have to learn.

489
00:34:06,544 --> 00:34:08,546
[slow beat playing]

490
00:34:11,674 --> 00:34:14,093
-Good morning, ma'am!
-[guard] Good morning, ma'am.

491
00:34:17,680 --> 00:34:20,266
Everyone, attention please.

492
00:34:20,975 --> 00:34:24,103
I want to introduce you
all to my daughter, Ivy.

493
00:34:24,979 --> 00:34:27,690
Starting today, she'll work
every day here after school.

494
00:34:27,774 --> 00:34:29,358
[all] Good morning, Ms. Ivy!

495
00:34:29,442 --> 00:34:31,027
I don't want any special treatment.

496
00:34:31,110 --> 00:34:32,236
Just Ivy.

497
00:34:32,320 --> 00:34:33,738
[woman] Are you grooming
your daughter, ma'am?

498
00:34:33,821 --> 00:34:35,031
Retiring anytime soon?

499
00:34:35,114 --> 00:34:37,492
No. Perhaps you'll retire first.

500
00:34:37,575 --> 00:34:39,285
[woman] I was just kidding, ma'am.

501
00:34:40,870 --> 00:34:44,165
Good morning. The meeting
is ready in 15 minutes at the board room.

502
00:34:45,333 --> 00:34:47,585
That's the bidding for the C5 project.

503
00:34:48,294 --> 00:34:49,295
I want you with me.

504
00:34:53,257 --> 00:34:56,219
Ivy? What are you waiting for? Now!

505
00:34:57,553 --> 00:35:02,433
Mr. De Leon,
our last bid is 88 million pesos.

506
00:35:03,810 --> 00:35:07,271
Ms. Aguas, there are
developments in the area.

507
00:35:07,939 --> 00:35:11,901
In the north side,
they established a mall.

508
00:35:11,984 --> 00:35:13,820
And in the south side,

509
00:35:13,903 --> 00:35:15,863
there will be a rail transit
in a prime location.

510
00:35:16,989 --> 00:35:19,033
What I am saying, Ms. Aguas,

511
00:35:19,117 --> 00:35:23,121
is that my property is really huge.

512
00:35:24,080 --> 00:35:27,792
And you're offering me
much less than what it's worth.

513
00:35:28,960 --> 00:35:33,464
It's our last bid,
Mr. De Leon. Take it or leave it.

514
00:35:35,091 --> 00:35:39,137
There are six other companies
that are bidding on my company.

515
00:35:39,220 --> 00:35:42,431
But I'm looking for
a more permanent relationship.

516
00:35:43,015 --> 00:35:47,186
I mean, a business
partnership with your company.

517
00:35:48,521 --> 00:35:52,441
I don't do partnerships.
I never believed in forever.

518
00:35:53,609 --> 00:35:56,195
It's never too late to believe in forever.

519
00:35:58,406 --> 00:36:01,868
Why don't we just schedule
another meeting between the two of us?

520
00:36:02,618 --> 00:36:06,706
I'll think about it.
Frankly, I don't see any point.

521
00:36:06,789 --> 00:36:10,710
Unless you give me a very good reason.

522
00:36:14,046 --> 00:36:15,965
Thank you very much
for your time, Mr. De Leon.

523
00:36:16,048 --> 00:36:18,509
I wish you good luck
with your six bidders.

524
00:36:18,593 --> 00:36:21,512
My next meeting is waiting. Excuse me.

525
00:36:26,893 --> 00:36:28,895
[slow beat playing]

526
00:36:29,812 --> 00:36:32,607
[secretary] Ma'am,
we didn't close the deal.

527
00:36:32,690 --> 00:36:34,692
The contractor is ready.

528
00:36:34,775 --> 00:36:36,194
Hold this.

529
00:36:37,653 --> 00:36:39,739
Five. Four.

530
00:36:39,822 --> 00:36:42,241
-Three. Two.
-[phone ringing]

531
00:36:46,746 --> 00:36:47,663
Answer it.

532
00:36:49,123 --> 00:36:52,126
-Hello, Mr. De Leon?
-Hello. May I speak

533
00:36:52,210 --> 00:36:53,836
<i>to Ms. Aguas, please?</i>

534
00:36:53,920 --> 00:36:55,963
<i>Because I'll never forgive myself</i>

535
00:36:56,047 --> 00:36:59,300
<i>if I let go of the chance</i>
<i>to work with someone as</i>

536
00:36:59,383 --> 00:37:00,384
beautiful as you.

537
00:37:01,928 --> 00:37:05,723
Okay. Meet me at my house, 8 PM.

538
00:37:05,806 --> 00:37:08,100
-Don't be late.
-I'll be there.

539
00:37:11,020 --> 00:37:12,146
You'll be there too.

540
00:37:16,275 --> 00:37:17,902
[slow beat playing]

541
00:37:20,404 --> 00:37:23,115
Thank you for having me
for dinner, Ms. Aguas.

542
00:37:23,199 --> 00:37:25,993
Mr. De Leon, call me Prianka.

543
00:37:26,077 --> 00:37:28,329
Then you can call me Teddy.

544
00:37:28,412 --> 00:37:29,497
[chuckles softly]

545
00:37:29,580 --> 00:37:31,999
Sure, Teddy Boy. Have a seat.

546
00:37:33,292 --> 00:37:34,335
Thank you.

547
00:37:42,551 --> 00:37:43,469
Oysters?

548
00:37:43,552 --> 00:37:47,223
They say eating oysters
on an empty stomach is not a good idea.

549
00:37:47,306 --> 00:37:48,557
[Prianka laughs]

550
00:37:52,019 --> 00:37:54,438
Casanova, the greatest lover,

551
00:37:54,522 --> 00:37:58,401
loved eating oysters for breakfast.

552
00:37:58,484 --> 00:38:01,362
It was his favorite aphrodisiac.

553
00:38:01,445 --> 00:38:04,490
[sensual music playing]

554
00:38:05,574 --> 00:38:07,910
Then, I better have an oyster.

555
00:38:11,580 --> 00:38:12,748
[slurps]

556
00:38:14,250 --> 00:38:16,961
[Prianka] We've had three meetings.

557
00:38:17,044 --> 00:38:19,672
I don't think you want to make me feel

558
00:38:19,755 --> 00:38:23,134
that you're just messing around,
Teddy Boy.

559
00:38:23,759 --> 00:38:24,885
Because you know

560
00:38:24,969 --> 00:38:27,346
I hate wasting time.

561
00:38:28,431 --> 00:38:29,515
I'm the same way.

562
00:38:30,391 --> 00:38:31,642
[chuckles]

563
00:38:32,476 --> 00:38:36,063
[Prianka] I believe that
when you know what you want,

564
00:38:36,147 --> 00:38:37,690
you should know how to get it.

565
00:38:38,482 --> 00:38:40,901
What do you want, Teddy Boy?

566
00:38:46,032 --> 00:38:47,116
More oysters?

567
00:38:48,284 --> 00:38:49,201
Yes.

568
00:38:50,286 --> 00:38:52,455
[clicks tongue]

569
00:38:52,538 --> 00:38:53,748
As for me…

570
00:38:54,957 --> 00:38:57,126
This is what I want.

571
00:38:58,461 --> 00:38:59,420
Of course.

572
00:39:00,463 --> 00:39:01,964
Of course.

573
00:39:05,384 --> 00:39:08,012
[slow beat playing]

574
00:39:17,438 --> 00:39:20,566
It was good
doing business with you, Mr. De Leon.

575
00:39:20,649 --> 00:39:22,360
I'm sorry, I have another meeting.

576
00:39:22,943 --> 00:39:24,487
Ivy will show you the way out.

577
00:39:24,570 --> 00:39:26,572
After you finish your dinner, of course.

578
00:39:31,410 --> 00:39:34,872
[Ivy] <i>She got what she wanted</i>
<i>at a price she dictated</i>

579
00:39:34,955 --> 00:39:36,707
<i>without a compromise.</i>

580
00:39:36,791 --> 00:39:39,627
<i>She put herself out there like bait.</i>

581
00:39:39,710 --> 00:39:42,838
<i>But didn't fall for her own trap.</i>

582
00:39:42,922 --> 00:39:46,634
That came from the projection
studies prepared by Ivy.

583
00:39:49,178 --> 00:39:50,471
Well?

584
00:39:50,554 --> 00:39:54,600
Uh, Ms. Prianka, based on the analyses--

585
00:39:54,683 --> 00:39:58,646
Well… Those analyses are obviously wrong.

586
00:39:59,814 --> 00:40:00,648
I'm sorry.

587
00:40:00,731 --> 00:40:03,401
Sorry is the most meaningless word for me.

588
00:40:03,484 --> 00:40:05,653
Do you know what I'd appreciate more?

589
00:40:05,736 --> 00:40:07,363
If you work harder.

590
00:40:08,739 --> 00:40:10,241
Try it.

591
00:40:12,368 --> 00:40:18,833
[Ivy] <i>Sometimes, I admire her.</i>
<i>Other times, she frustrates me.</i>

592
00:40:19,667 --> 00:40:20,709
<i>But now…</i>

593
00:40:21,710 --> 00:40:23,671
<i>I want to be just like her.</i>

594
00:40:24,713 --> 00:40:29,802
[instrumental theme music playing]

595
00:40:57,288 --> 00:40:59,373
[Ivy] And that will ensure
the success of this project.

596
00:41:01,709 --> 00:41:04,044
So, where do I sign, Ms. Aguas?

597
00:41:06,672 --> 00:41:09,884
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda playing]

598
00:41:24,106 --> 00:41:31,030
<i>♪ Let her cry, for she's a lady</i>
<i>For she's a lady ♪</i>

599
00:41:31,113 --> 00:41:36,994
<i>♪ Let her dream, for she's a child</i>
<i>For she's a child ♪</i>

600
00:41:37,870 --> 00:41:41,373
<i>♪ Let the rain</i>
<i>Let the rain fall down upon her ♪</i>

601
00:41:41,457 --> 00:41:45,836
[Mia] Didn't I say no?
Quit bothering me! I said no!

602
00:41:45,920 --> 00:41:47,129
[man] You don't have to pretend.

603
00:41:47,213 --> 00:41:49,006
-[Mia] Stop!
-[man] I know you want it too.

604
00:41:49,089 --> 00:41:51,425
-[Mia] I don't! Stop!
-[man] Come on!

605
00:41:51,509 --> 00:41:53,093
-[man] You want this, right?
-[Mia] I don't!

606
00:41:53,177 --> 00:41:56,514
-You want this too, don't you?
-Stop it! Get off me!

607
00:41:56,597 --> 00:41:58,891
[Ivy] If Mia says she doesn't want to…

608
00:41:58,974 --> 00:42:02,311
-[man] Ouch. Ma'am.
-That means no! Understood?

609
00:42:02,394 --> 00:42:04,605
[Ivy] Mia? Go back to work.

610
00:42:04,688 --> 00:42:07,316
-Yes, ma'am.
-And you? You're fired.

611
00:42:07,399 --> 00:42:08,317
[groans]

612
00:42:09,777 --> 00:42:11,445
-Guard!
-That hurts.

613
00:42:11,529 --> 00:42:12,738
Take him outside.

614
00:42:12,821 --> 00:42:15,074
Starting today,
he is no longer our employee.

615
00:42:15,157 --> 00:42:16,700
All right, ma'am. Come here.

616
00:42:25,125 --> 00:42:27,711
-Ma'am?
-Yes?

617
00:42:27,795 --> 00:42:33,801
I wanted to thank you
for saving me earlier.

618
00:42:34,843 --> 00:42:37,471
Mia, having good manners is important.

619
00:42:37,555 --> 00:42:42,518
But I'd like it more if you
learned to defend yourself.

620
00:42:43,852 --> 00:42:48,816
We women shouldn't wait
for a knight in shining armor.

621
00:42:48,899 --> 00:42:52,486
Learn how to protect yourself.

622
00:42:53,070 --> 00:42:53,904
Yes, ma'am.

623
00:42:54,947 --> 00:42:55,781
You may go.

624
00:43:00,911 --> 00:43:04,039
[Ivy] <i>Ms. Prianka always said…</i>

625
00:43:04,123 --> 00:43:08,836
<i>that one should be patient</i>
<i>to achieve justice.</i>

626
00:43:09,587 --> 00:43:12,506
<i>I have to wait for the right moment.</i>

627
00:43:13,382 --> 00:43:15,342
<i>I've waited for so long.</i>

628
00:43:16,969 --> 00:43:21,098
<i>And even though the whole world</i>
<i>knows me as Ivy Aguas…</i>

629
00:43:23,142 --> 00:43:24,643
<i>a different name…</i>

630
00:43:25,686 --> 00:43:27,396
<i>with a different origin…</i>

631
00:43:28,105 --> 00:43:30,608
<i>and a different birthday…</i>

632
00:43:32,151 --> 00:43:34,612
<i>Lily isn't dead.</i>

633
00:43:35,487 --> 00:43:39,867
<i>She's been waiting</i>
<i>for the right moment to strike.</i>

634
00:43:39,950 --> 00:43:43,203
Happy birthday, Lily.

635
00:43:43,829 --> 00:43:46,373
[instrumental theme music playing]

636
00:44:11,398 --> 00:44:13,359
Ivy? You're home early.

637
00:44:14,276 --> 00:44:18,656
You're leaving, Ms. Prianka?
Do you want me to accompany you?

638
00:44:18,739 --> 00:44:20,491
No. I'll be fine.

639
00:44:27,122 --> 00:44:28,957
-Nanny Carlotta?
-Yes?

640
00:44:29,041 --> 00:44:31,293
Do you know where Ms. Prianka is going?

641
00:44:31,377 --> 00:44:35,798
-She didn't come to work today.
-She didn't say.

642
00:44:35,881 --> 00:44:37,216
Only that it was a personal trip.

643
00:44:38,008 --> 00:44:40,052
But, you know, it's been going
on for six months now.

644
00:44:40,135 --> 00:44:42,554
She leaves every Thursday without fail.

645
00:44:45,140 --> 00:44:47,226
[suspenseful music playing]

646
00:44:49,061 --> 00:44:51,605
[Emilia] <i>My condolences,</i>
<i>Mrs. Cruz. I'm sorry for your loss.</i>

647
00:44:51,688 --> 00:44:53,065
<i>It must've been so painful for you.</i>

648
00:44:53,148 --> 00:44:54,900
-Get out of here!
-Mom! Please stop!

649
00:44:54,983 --> 00:44:57,861
[Camia] <i>You killed my husband!</i>
<i>You killed my husband!</i>

650
00:44:57,945 --> 00:44:59,905
-[shushes]
-[man] <i>Hey!</i>

651
00:45:00,572 --> 00:45:01,865
<i>Run!</i>

652
00:45:02,991 --> 00:45:03,992
Mom?

653
00:45:13,460 --> 00:45:16,380
[Carlotta] Ms. Prianka? Ms. Prianka?

654
00:45:17,381 --> 00:45:20,175
Ms. Prianka? Ms. Prianka?

655
00:45:21,093 --> 00:45:23,846
Ivy! Ivy!

656
00:45:26,140 --> 00:45:27,808
-Nanny Carlotta?
-[Carlotta crying] Ivy!

657
00:45:28,976 --> 00:45:29,810
What happened?

658
00:45:34,648 --> 00:45:38,068
Ms. Prianka? Ms. Prianka?! Ms. Prianka?

659
00:45:38,152 --> 00:45:39,903
Ms. Prianka?

660
00:45:41,447 --> 00:45:45,284
She has Stage IV ovarian
cancer. She was diagnosed too late.

661
00:45:45,367 --> 00:45:49,079
She refuses to have regular check-ups,

662
00:45:49,163 --> 00:45:51,123
even though she's shown
symptoms for months.

663
00:45:53,125 --> 00:45:55,961
[doctor] <i>It's been six months</i>
<i>since she was diagnosed with cancer.</i>

664
00:45:56,920 --> 00:45:58,589
<i>We do chemotherapy every Thursday,</i>

665
00:45:58,672 --> 00:46:01,508
<i>but she refuses to stay in the hospital.</i>

666
00:46:04,094 --> 00:46:06,013
[coughs]

667
00:46:06,096 --> 00:46:07,931
[wheezing]

668
00:46:11,435 --> 00:46:14,855
[somber music playing]

669
00:46:14,938 --> 00:46:16,231
[coughs]

670
00:46:50,724 --> 00:46:51,808
[weakly] You know…

671
00:46:54,353 --> 00:46:56,104
you've been a good child.

672
00:46:57,356 --> 00:46:59,691
That's the first time you praised me.

673
00:47:04,029 --> 00:47:05,739
[Prianka] Ivy.

674
00:47:07,783 --> 00:47:10,118
I may not show it…

675
00:47:12,996 --> 00:47:15,874
but I love you as my own daughter.

676
00:47:18,669 --> 00:47:20,087
For a long time…

677
00:47:21,380 --> 00:47:23,173
you gave me purpose…

678
00:47:25,008 --> 00:47:28,470
to keep living.

679
00:47:30,138 --> 00:47:35,185
But now, I can finally let go.

680
00:47:36,603 --> 00:47:39,940
No. Ms. Prianka, no.

681
00:47:40,566 --> 00:47:42,276
No, no.

682
00:47:43,151 --> 00:47:44,152
[sighs heavily]

683
00:47:45,612 --> 00:47:47,322
You can't give up.

684
00:47:47,406 --> 00:47:49,908
You said you don't want
anyone dying on your watch.

685
00:47:49,992 --> 00:47:52,661
So, you can't give up. You can't die.

686
00:47:53,870 --> 00:47:56,123
There is no point, Ivy.

687
00:47:57,583 --> 00:48:00,711
Death is inevitable.

688
00:48:00,794 --> 00:48:03,380
I've kept my end of the deal.

689
00:48:04,131 --> 00:48:05,674
Now…

690
00:48:07,050 --> 00:48:08,468
it's your turn.

691
00:48:09,136 --> 00:48:14,266
Remember everything I taught you.

692
00:48:15,892 --> 00:48:19,479
Do what you must do.

693
00:48:20,105 --> 00:48:21,607
[shushes]

694
00:48:21,690 --> 00:48:23,817
Make them pay.

695
00:48:25,277 --> 00:48:28,697
-Ms. Prianka? Ms. Prianka?
-[Prianka groaning]

696
00:48:30,240 --> 00:48:31,116
Ma'am?

697
00:48:33,660 --> 00:48:35,078
Where does it hurt?

698
00:48:40,459 --> 00:48:41,543
Ma'am?

699
00:48:42,502 --> 00:48:43,378
Ms. Prianka?

700
00:48:43,462 --> 00:48:46,757
Ma'am? Ms. Prianka?

701
00:48:46,840 --> 00:48:48,091
Ma'am?

702
00:48:50,093 --> 00:48:51,428
Ma'am?

703
00:48:53,221 --> 00:48:54,348
[sniffles]

704
00:48:54,431 --> 00:48:55,682
Ma'am?

705
00:48:59,227 --> 00:49:01,271
[Ivy] <i>I made a promise to my parents.</i>

706
00:49:03,774 --> 00:49:05,984
<i>Now, I promise you.</i>

707
00:49:07,277 --> 00:49:09,071
<i>I'll make them pay.</i>

708
00:49:12,866 --> 00:49:15,994
[dramatic music playing]

709
00:49:27,923 --> 00:49:29,800
[Ivy] <i>Hello, Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

710
00:49:30,884 --> 00:49:32,094
<i>I'm back.</i>

711
00:49:33,136 --> 00:49:34,346
<i>Who's that?</i>

712
00:49:34,429 --> 00:49:37,683
[Ivy] <i>To all of them, Lily is dead.</i>

713
00:49:37,766 --> 00:49:42,396
[Carlotta]<i> Ivy is here to seek</i>
<i>justice for Lily's parents.</i>

714
00:49:42,479 --> 00:49:45,023
[Ivy] <i>Emilia is the key</i>
<i>to what happened to Mom.</i>

715
00:49:45,107 --> 00:49:48,985
<i>But you are the key to Emilia.</i>
<i>I'll start with you.</i>

716
00:49:49,069 --> 00:49:50,195
[townspeople cheering]

717
00:49:50,278 --> 00:49:55,367
[Diego] <i>I still believe</i>
<i>that Lily will come back.</i>

718
00:49:55,450 --> 00:49:56,451
<i>For you.</i>

719
00:49:56,535 --> 00:49:59,079
[theme music playing]
